# ############################################################################
# #  THIS FILE IS COMMITTED TO GIT AND PUBLISHED ON GITHUB.                  #
# #  Real values go in  .env.local  — which is gitignored.                   #
# #  Anything you paste below this line becomes public.                      #
# ############################################################################
#
# Every line here is a commented-out placeholder on purpose. If you find
# yourself pasting a real key, URL or token into this file, stop: you want
# .env.local. The app reads .env.local; it never reads this file.
#
# Without these the app serves the built-in sample menu from
# src/lib/seed-menu.ts.

# Supabase → Project Settings → API
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Server-only. Bypasses RLS — needed for admin writes in Phase 2.
# Never prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never import it into a client component.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Shared password for /kitchen. Minimum 8 characters.
KITCHEN_PASSWORD=

# Order emails, relayed through a Google Apps Script web app so the mail comes
# from the kitchen's own Gmail address. See google-apps-script/Code.gs for the
# script and its deployment steps.
#
# The /exec URL of the deployment. It is world-callable by design — Apps Script
# requires "Anyone" access for an unauthenticated server to POST — so the secret
# below is the only thing preventing someone who finds the URL from sending mail
# as the kitchen. Use a long random string and set the SAME value in the script's
# Script Properties. Without both, the app simply sends no email.
# APPS_SCRIPT_EMAIL_URL=
# APPS_SCRIPT_EMAIL_SECRET=

# Public origin, used to build OAuth and email sign-in redirect URLs.
# Also used for the order link inside emails, so set it before going live.
# Optional in development — it is derived from the request headers when unset.
# Set it in production: behind a proxy the Host header is the internal name.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://joysfood.example.com

# Razorpay. Only the key id may be exposed to the browser.
# Dashboard → Settings → API Keys. Test keys are prefixed rzp_test_ and the app
# shows a "test mode" banner on the payment panel while they are in use.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
#
# A DIFFERENT secret from the key secret above: Dashboard → Settings → Webhooks,
# where you set it yourself when creating the webhook. Signs the raw request
# body. Without it the webhook route returns 503 and refuses to act, because an
# unverifiable payment event is worse than a missed one.
# Webhook URL: https://your-domain/api/webhooks/razorpay
# Subscribe to: payment.captured, payment.failed
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

